/**
 * @mainpage Solaris Software &mdash; API Reference
 *
 * @tableofcontents
 *
 * @section intro_sec Overview
 *
 * **Solaris** is the open-source avionics firmware of
 * <a href="https://uvigoaerotech.com/">UVigo Aerotech</a>, built on
 * <a href="https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/stable/">ESP-IDF</a>
 * for the **ESP32-S3**. It provides reusable sensor drivers and a small
 * framework &mdash; the **Solaris Packet Protocol (SPP)** &mdash; for hardware
 * abstraction, in-flight data flow and telemetry.
 *
 * This site is the reference for the C API: every file, function, struct and
 * macro, generated from the source comments. For the narrative documentation
 * (architecture, design rationale, guides) see the
 * <a href="/">Solaris documentation site</a>.
 *
 * @section entry_sec Entry point
 *
 * The application is deliberately tiny: it wires the ESP32-S3 HAL port into
 * the finite state machine and then ticks it forever.
 *
 * @code{.c}
 * void app_main(void)
 * {
 *     const SPP_HalPort_t *p_halPorts = SPP_PORTS_ESP32S3_getHalPorts();
 *     (void)FSM_init((void *)p_halPorts);
 *     while (1) {
 *         FSM_tick();
 *     }
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * Everything else &mdash; sensor sampling, packet routing, logging, downlink
 * &mdash; is driven from the FSM (@ref fsm.h) through the publish/subscribe
 * core (@ref pubsub.h).
 *
 * @section arch_sec The SPP framework
 *
 * SPP is layered so the same core and services run on real hardware, on a
 * host build, or against simulated sensors.
 *
 * @subsection core_sub Core
 *
 * - **Packet** &mdash; the on-the-wire telemetry unit and its headers.
 *   See @ref packet.h, @ref commonbit.h.
 * - **Publish / Subscribe** &mdash; decouples producers (sensors) from
 *   consumers (datalogger, downlink, FSM) via KPID subscriptions.
 *   See @ref pubsub.h, @ref core.h.
 * - **Common types** &mdash; fixed-width types and return codes shared by
 *   every module. See @ref types.h, @ref returnTypes.h, @ref version.h.
 *
 * @subsection hal_sub HAL &amp; ports
 *
 * The HAL (@ref hal.h) declares the buses and peripherals the services need;
 * a *port* implements them for a target. The ESP32-S3 port lives under
 * @ref halEsp32.h / @ref macrosEsp32.h.
 *
 * - **SPI** &mdash; shared bus + per-device handles. See @ref spi.h.
 * - **UART** &mdash; console / devkit link. See @ref uart.h.
 * - **GPIO** &mdash; data-ready and IRQ lines. See @ref gpio.h.
 * - **Storage** &mdash; SD card / filesystem. See @ref storage.h.
 * - **Time** &mdash; monotonic clock and delays. See @ref time.h.
 *
 * @subsection svc_sub Services
 *
 * | Module                 | Role                                             |
 * |------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
 * | @ref fsm.h             | Hierarchical finite state machine (orchestrator) |
 * | @ref databank.h        | Packet pool / allocator                          |
 * | @ref datalogger.h      | Persists packets to the SD card                  |
 * | @ref log.h             | Structured logging service                       |
 * | @ref bmp390.h          | BMP390 barometric pressure + altitude            |
 * | @ref icm20948.h        | ICM-20948 9-axis IMU with on-chip DMP            |
 * | MAX-M10M-20B.h         | u-blox MAX-M10 GNSS receiver                     |
 * | @ref sx1262.h          | SX1262 LoRa downlink (work in progress)          |
 *
 * @subsection ext_sub External
 *
 * - **Encryption** &mdash; AES-128-GCM for the telemetry link, compiled in
 *   only when `SPP_ENCRYPTION` is set. See @ref encryption.h, @ref cipher.h.
 *
 * @section hw_sec Reference hardware
 *
 * | Component  | Device    | Bus       | Notes                         |
 * |------------|-----------|-----------|-------------------------------|
 * | MCU        | ESP32-S3  | &mdash;   | ESP-IDF, ESP32-S3 target      |
 * | IMU        | ICM-20948 | SPI2_HOST | DMP FIFO, GPIO data-ready     |
 * | Barometer  | BMP390    | SPI2_HOST | interrupt-driven              |
 * | GNSS       | MAX-M10M  | UART      | NMEA / UBX                    |
 * | Downlink   | SX1262    | SPI + DIO | LoRa, work in progress        |
 *
 * The authoritative pin map (SPI CIPO/COPI/CLK, chip-selects, IRQ lines) is
 * defined in @ref macrosEsp32.h.
 *
 * @section build_sec Building
 *
 * @code{.sh}
 * cd solaris-v2
 * idf.py set-target esp32s3
 * idf.py build
 * @endcode
 *
 * Service inclusion is controlled with CMake options, e.g.
 * `idf.py build -DSPP_SERVICE_ICM20948=OFF`. See `compiler/spp/CMakeLists.txt`.
 *
